-- An EVERY's IN roll and its WHO or WHOSE filter are not among its own
-- slots: the roll call reads them in the environment the EVERY is written
-- in, before any member's obligation is armed. So THE ARMING there names
-- an arming only when the EVERY sits under a HENCE or LEST, where the
-- hand-off bound one; at the top level it is refused (refusal 8 of
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.1.1, card B1c, RULED 2026-10-24). Each of
-- the three used to check clean and be refused by the run on every input.
--
-- The two filters also report that `AT MOST` is ambiguous. That is not part
-- of refusal 8: a refused lifecycle value under an overloaded operator does
-- the same under refusal 1 (THE JOIN PLUS 1 at the top level, with the
-- prelude imported), because the refusal is raised inside every
-- candidate's branch, so no candidate comes out free of errors.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS lname IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS tname IS A STRING
                 since IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant WITH tname IS "Alice", since IS 0
bob         MEANS Tenant WITH tname IS "Bob",   since IS 20
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Actor
`tenants by` MEANS IF n GREATER THAN 10 THEN LIST alice ELSE tenants

-- refused: THE ARMING in the IN roll of a top-level EVERY
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll at the top` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN (`tenants by` THE ARMING)
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 10

-- refused: THE ARMING in the WHO filter of a top-level EVERY
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`who at the top` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        WHO    t's since AT MOST THE ARMING
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 10

-- refused: THE ARMING in the WHOSE filter of a top-level EVERY
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`whose at the top` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        WHOSE  since AT MOST THE ARMING
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 10

-- not refused: the same roll and filter under the landlord's HENCE, where
-- THE ARMING is when the landlord's obligation was entered
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll under a HENCE` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN (`tenants by` THE ARMING)
               WHOSE  since AT MOST THE ARMING
               MUST   Sign t
               WITHIN 10)

-- not refused: the EVERY's own act WITHIN and join line
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own slots at the top` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 10)
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        WITHIN 0 OF (THE ARMING PLUS 20)
        HENCE  FULFILLED
